{"shortDescription":"Asia's spot fuel oil premiums climbed further on Monday, with bids for key grades trekking higher from the previous session as sentiment remained supported by supply uncertainties in the Middle East.Singapore's 380-cst high sulphur fuel oil (HSFO) cash differential extended gains to above $56 a met…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Asia's spot fuel oil premiums climbed further on Monday, with bids for key grades trekking higher from the previous session as sentiment remained supported by supply uncertainties in the Middle East."]},{"type":"p","children":["Singapore's 380-cst high sulphur fuel oil (HSFO) cash differential extended gains to above $56 a metric ton over cargo quotes, holding at over a five-month high."]},{"type":"p","children":["Meanwhile, very low sulphur fuel oil's (VLSFO) premium also climbed, with bids strengthening further into October, though the strength remained capped versus HSFO's recent rally. The cash differential was pegged at above $35 a ton."]},{"type":"p","children":["Margins showed a largely similar trend, with the VLSFO crack (LFO05SGBRTCMc1) hovering near a premium of $20 a barrel at the Asia close on Monday, broadly steady from last Friday. HSFO margins were more elevated, with 380-cst HSFO's crack (FO380BRTCKMc1) rising to a discount near $1.90 a barrel."]},{"type":"p","children":["As for spot sales, Indonesia's Pertamina offered residual fuels for loading in October, including two cargoes of decant oil and one cargo of low-sulphur waxy residue. The tender closed on Monday, according to market sources."]},{"type":"p","children":["BUNKER SALES"]},{"type":"p","children":["Marine fuel sales in Singapore edged higher for a fourth consecutive month in August on the back of resilient demand, official data showed on Monday."]},{"type":"p","children":["Sales totalled 4.77 million metric tons in August, up 0.7% month on month, though down 3.9% year on year, data from the Maritime and Port Authority of Singapore showed."]},{"type":"p","children":["OTHER NEWS"]},{"type":"p","children":["- Oil prices continued their surge, rising more than 3% on Monday, after new strikes on Saudi Arabian energy infrastructure and attacks on ships in the Middle East compounded supply concerns."]},{"type":"p","children":["- Arab states in the Gulf called off a meeting with Iran planned for Monday, while Yemen's Houthis launched a new attack on Saudi Arabia after fighting that has extended the Middle East war to another theatre and further jeopardised global oil supplies."]},{"type":"p","children":["- Saudi Arabia will run out of oil stocks for exports if it doesn't restart its major pipeline to the Red Sea within days, leading to a loss of up to 4% of global supply, Saudi oil buyers and traders said."]},{"type":"p","children":["- Nigerian billionaire Aliko Dangote on Monday launched Africa's largest share sale yet with the initial public offering of his oil refinery, opening up ownership of the plant to retail investors and raising money for its expansion."]},{"type":"p","children":["WINDOW TRADES"]},{"type":"p","children":["- 180-cst HSFO: No trade."]},{"type":"p","children":["- 380-cst HSFO: Two trades."]},{"type":"p","children":["- 0.5% VLSFO: No trade."]},{"type":"p","children":["ASSESSMENTS"]},{"type":"table","children":[{"type":"table-body","children":[{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["FUEL OIL"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["CASH ($/T)"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["ASIA CLOSE"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["CHANGE"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["PREV CLOSE"]}]},{